Chapter 11: Worked Example – Belief Fusion on a Probability Simplex

We illustrate the entire theory on the simplest non‑trivial manifold: the open probability simplex \Delta^{d-1} = \{p\in\mathbb{R}^d : p_i>0, \sum p_i=1\}.

11.1 Geometry and Metric

Take \mathcal{M} = \Delta^{d-1} with the Fisher metric:

g_{ij}(p) = \frac{\delta_{ij}}{p_i} + \frac{1}{p_d} \quad (\text{in some coordinates}).
\]  

This metric is complete under the inherited geometry; geodesic distance equals the Bhattacharyya distance.

11.2 Potential from Local Beliefs

Suppose m modules provide prior distributions q^{(k)}\in\Delta^{d-1}, k=1,\dots,m. Define the cognitive potential

\Phi(p) = \sum_{k=1}^m w_k D_{KL}(p \| q^{(k)}),

where w_k>0 are weights and D_{KL}(p\|q) = \sum_i p_i \log(p_i/q_i). This potential is strictly convex in the dually flat coordinates \theta_i = \log(p_i/p_d); it is proper and real‑analytic on \Delta^{d-1}.

11.3 Gradient Flow

The gradient flow with respect to the Fisher metric is equivalent to the replicator dynamics:

\dot{p}_i = p_i \left( \sum_k w_k \log \frac{q_i^{(k)}}{p_i} - \sum_j p_j \sum_k w_k \log \frac{q_j^{(k)}}{p_j} \right).
\]  

This flow has a unique global minimum at the weighted geometric mean

p^*_i \propto \prod_k (q_i^{(k)})^{w_k}.
\]  

All trajectories converge exponentially to p^* (Theorem 6.2, with KL inequality, guarantees convergence; here convexity gives exponential rate). Thus autonomous coherence holds.

11.4 Soft Sheaf Consensus

If we regard each q^{(k)} as the state of a local module on a trivial sheaf, the potential above is exactly \Phi_{\text{loc}} + \lambda D with D_{KL} as divergence. The global minimum p^* is the optimal soft global section, balancing all prior beliefs. No central coordinator is required—the gradient flow finds it.

11.5 Topological Features

In this convex landscape, the sublevel sets are contractible, so no non‑trivial persistent homology appears. However, if we add a non‑convex perturbation (e.g., a bimodal prior), \Phi becomes a Morse function on a compactified simplex, and the flow can undergo Morse transitions between minima—representing a shift from one belief cluster to another.

This simple example confirms that the axioms are not vacuous and that the theory’s conclusions are realised in a tangible setting.

