Appendix G: Glossary of Symbols and Conventions

· \mathcal{M}: Smooth, connected, paracompact Riemannian manifold (cognitive space).
· g: Riemannian metric on \mathcal{M}.
· \Phi: Cognitive potential, \Phi:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}, proper, real‑analytic, bounded below.
· \nabla_g: Gradient operator with respect to g.
· d_g: Geodesic distance induced by g.
· \operatorname{Hess}_g\Phi: Hessian of \Phi with respect to the Levi‑Civita connection.
· \omega(x_0): Omega‑limit set of the trajectory starting at x_0.
· \varphi: KL function (concave, etc.).
· \tau: Time step in JKO scheme.
· D_{ij}: Divergence measure between modules i and j.
· \mathcal{M}_\epsilon: Sublevel set \{x : \Phi(x)\le \epsilon\}.


